%% The test is a gate — Pipelines Fundamentals, lab exercise 3 ("You'll end with").
%% Top row: with the toggle set to false the unit test fails on the API's 409, the run stops, and
%% build-image, image-report and deploy are skipped (no image is built). Bottom row: with the toggle
%% back to true, unit-test passes and the run carries on through build, report and deploy.
%% Shape (diagram-size-guard): TB of two LR subgraphs joined only container-to-container (the
%% invisible link), so each direction LR is honoured; longest chain 4 nodes.
flowchart TB
  subgraph RED["toggle false: the run goes red"]
    direction LR
    R1["unit-test<br/>API answers 409"] -->|"stops"| R2["build-image, image-report,<br/>deploy: skipped"]
  end
  subgraph GREEN["toggle back to true: the run goes green"]
    direction LR
    G1["unit-test<br/>Failures: 0"] --> G2["build-image"]
    G2 --> G3["image-report"]
    G3 --> G4["deploy"]
  end
  RED ~~~ GREEN
  classDef bad fill:#fce8e6,stroke:#c5221f,color:#a50e0e;
  classDef skip fill:#f3f3f3,stroke:#888,color:#555,stroke-dasharray: 4 3;
  classDef done fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#137333,color:#0d652d;
  class R1 bad;
  class R2 skip;
  class G1,G2,G3,G4 done;
